{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Ct26wPgp5puJk6Ntw5je9c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Po6GWztU94UYxmsY1CE6NF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\nYour focus areas: **Methods** and **Experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\nTitle: \"When Less Cleaning Hurts: An Empirical Study of Adaptive Importance Weighting for Contaminated Pretraining\"\n\nThe paper studies adaptive per-batch selection of the exponent b in detect-and-reweight pretraining (wi = (1-qi)^b). Two strategies are compared:\n1. Dual-constrained b* (min-intervention): smallest b satisfying α_eff ≥ τ subject to ESS ≥ n_min\n2. ESS-only b* (max-intervention): largest b satisfying ESS ≥ n_min\n\nKey findings:\n- ESS-only adaptive b* outperforms grid-best fixed b (17.635 vs 17.651 PPL) and dual-constrained (17.635 vs 17.650)\n- α_eff quality constraint is harmful under imperfect detection (AUC=0.939), inert under strong detection (AUC=0.986)\n- τ shows high sensitivity with no robust operating region\n- Recommended: ESS-only adaptive b* with n_min=2 as tuning-free default\n\n## Experimental Setup\n- Primary model: Qwen3-0.6B (600M params), Scale validation: Llama-3.2-3B\n- Contaminated FineWeb with controlled synthetic injection at ρ ∈ {0.4, 0.6}, 200M tokens\n- Detectors: TF-IDF+LR (AUC=0.939), ModernBERT (AUC=0.986)\n- Evaluation: holdout PPL, downstream MMLU/HellaSwag for 3B model\n- Baselines: Uniform, Grid-best, Detect-and-remove, Random reweight, Golden Ratio oracle\n- Seed variance established at 0.005 PPL from 3-seed uniform baseline\n\n## Key Tables from Paper\n\nTable 1 (Complete comparison, ρ=0.4, seed 42):\n- Golden Ratio oracle: 17.625 (-0.065)\n- n_min=1: 17.632 (-0.058), mean b*=6.80\n- ESS-only: 17.635 (-0.055), mean b*=4.15\n- Dual (τ=0.8): 17.650 (-0.040), mean b*=1.40\n- Grid-best (b=0.5): 17.651 (-0.039)\n- Uniform: 17.690\n- Random reweight: 17.710 (+0.020)\n\nTable 2 (Multi-seed, only for uniform/grid-best/dual):\n- Uniform: mean 17.693, std 0.005\n- Grid-best: mean 17.646, std 0.006\n- Dual: mean 17.651, std 0.007\n\nTable 3 (Fixed-b sweep): U-shaped, optimal at b=0.5, sharp degradation for b≥1.0\n\nTable 5 (Detector quality interaction):\n- TF-IDF+LR: Dual 17.650, ESS-only 17.635, gap 0.015\n- ModernBERT: Dual 17.640, ESS-only 17.638, gap 0.002\n\nTable 6 (τ sweep): PPL monotonically increases from 17.640 (τ=0.5) to 17.800 (τ=0.95)\n\nTable 7 (n_min ablation): n_min=1 best (17.632), n_min≥3 degrades to uniform\n\nTable 9 (ρ=0.6): Dual 18.550 (-0.250), Grid b=0.5: 18.500 (-0.300) — dual underperforms fixed b\n\nTable 10 (Llama-3.2-3B): Effect shrinks to 0.020 PPL, downstream metrics indistinguishable\n\n## Review Context (Imagined Experiment Coverage)\n\nThe review_context.yaml lists these planned experiments. Check which ones the paper actually reports vs omits:\n1. Uniform baselines × 3 seeds ✓ (Table 2)\n2. Grid-b sweep seed42 ✓ (Table 3)\n3. Adaptive_fix × 3 seeds ✓ (Table 2, partial — only dual, no ESS-only multi-seed)\n4. ESS-only adaptive baseline ✓ (Table 4)\n5. τ sweep ✓ (Table 6)\n6. Golden Ratio oracle ✓ (Table 1)\n7. n_min=1 ablation ✓ (Table 7)\n8. Grid-b low (b=0.1/0.2/0.3) × 3 seeds — partially (Table 3 has seed42, multi-seed for low-b not reported)\n9. ρ=0.6 datagen + uniform + adaptive + grid ✓ (Table 9, but missing ESS-only at ρ=0.6)\n10. n_min=4, n_min=5 ablations ✓ (Table 7)\n11. batch_size=8, 16 ✓ (Table 8)\n12. ModernBERT detector + training ✓ (Table 5)\n13. Cross-generator ✓ (§6.4, but only text, no table)\n14. Llama-3.2-3B ✓ (Table 10)\n15. Detect-and-remove baseline ✓ (§6.7)\n16. Random reweight baseline ✓ (Table 1)\n17. Domain-skewed injection ✓ (§6.5, no table)\n18. Downstream eval ✓ (Table 10)\n\nNotable omissions: ESS-only multi-seed, ESS-only at ρ=0.6, low-b multi-seed\n\n## Your Task\n\nEvaluate the paper on:\n\n1. **Methodological soundness**: Are the formulations (dual-constrained, ESS-only) well-defined? Is the experimental methodology rigorous? Are the statistical claims justified given the effect sizes and seed variance?\n\n2. **Experimental thoroughness**: Coverage of ablations, baselines, sensitivity analyses. Are there critical missing experiments? Are the effect sizes convincing?\n\n3. **Reproducibility**: Is there enough detail to reproduce?\n\n4. **Weaknesses in methods/experiments**: Identify specific issues.\n\nProvide your assessment in this format:\n\n### R1 Assessment: Methods & Experiments\n\n**Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n\n**Strengths**\n- S1: ...\n- S2: ...\n- ...\n\n**Weaknesses**\n- W1: ...\n- W2: ...\n- ...\n\n**Questions for Authors**\n- Q1: ...\n- ...\n\n**Missing Experiments**\n- ...\n\n**Preliminary Score**: X/6\n**Confidence**: X/5\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35626,"cache_read_input_tokens":22936,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35626},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e76514d-f28c-4641-af3a-08051cc17412","uuid":"8eb6d14c-81ee-4450-be7b-8b4d14ec5588"}
